import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Delete Your Sk8tics Account"
  description="How to delete a Sk8tics account and everything in it, from inside the app, or through the contact form if you can't sign in."
>

  <p class="eyebrow">Account deletion</p>
  <h1>Delete your Sk8tics account</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Delete it in the app: tap <strong>Account</strong> at the top of any
    screen, then <strong>Delete my account</strong> at the bottom of the sheet.
  </p>

  <h2 id="before-you-go">Before you go</h2>
  <p>
    If you only want a coach to stop seeing your log, you do not need to delete
    your account. Remove them on the <strong>Coaches</strong> screen: tap
    <strong>Remove access</strong>, then <strong>Remove</strong>. You keep your
    account and your history, and access stops the moment you do.
  </p>
  <p>
    The run-through scores and competition results that the coach entered
    themselves stay visible to that coach. Your log, your drills and the
    competition results you recorded yourself stop being visible to them.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete it in the app</h2>
  <p>
    Open Sk8tics and tap <strong>Account</strong> at the top of any screen.
    Scroll to the bottom of the sheet, type your username where it says
    <strong>Type <em>your username</em> to confirm</strong>, then tap
    <strong>Delete my account</strong>.
  </p>
  <div class="note accent">
    <strong>It happens immediately and cannot be undone.</strong>
    We keep no copy, and there is no grace period to change your mind.
  </div>

  <h2>If you can't sign in</h2>
  <p>
    Only if you can't get into the app, use the <a href="/support#contact">contact form</a> with the
    email address on the account, and say <em>Delete my Sk8tics account</em>
    in the message. Include your username if you remember it. We reply to that
    address to confirm before we delete anything.
  </p>
  <p>
    A parent or guardian may make this request for a child&rsquo;s account. Say
    so in the message and give the child&rsquo;s username; we do not need the
    child&rsquo;s agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li>Your sign-in and your email address.</li>
    <li>Your profile &mdash; username, name, discipline.</li>
    <li>Every practice session and every element mark in it.</li>
    <li>Your programs and their planned content.</li>
    <li>Every run-through score a coach recorded for you, and their notes.</li>
    <li>Every competition record saved against you.</li>
    <li>Your links to coaches.</li>
    <li>Any device registered for notifications.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you are a coach, the records you wrote <em>about other skaters</em> are
    deleted too, since they are part of your account.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not affected</h2>
  <p>
    Competition protocols published by Skate Ontario and skatingresults.ca are
    their documents on their websites. Deleting a Sk8tics account removes our
    copy of a result; it has no bearing on the official record, which we do not
    control and cannot change.
  </p>

  <h2 id="partial">Deleting only some of your data</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li>
      <strong>One day:</strong> on the Log tab, open the day, tap
      <strong>Clear this day</strong>, then <strong>Clear day</strong>. This
      clears the session for the program you have open on that day, and every
      element mark in it. Sessions for your other programs that day, and drills,
      are not touched. A coach&rsquo;s run-through scores for that day are kept,
      but are no longer tied to the day&rsquo;s session.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A program:</strong> on the Programs tab, edit the program, tap
      <strong>Delete program</strong>, then <strong>Delete</strong>. This deletes
      the program, its planned elements, every session logged against it, and
      any run-through scores and competition results attached to it, including
      ones a coach entered.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A season:</strong> on the Programs tab, tap the
      <strong>&times;</strong> on the season heading, then
      <strong>Delete season</strong>. This does the same as deleting a program,
      for every program in that season.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Competition results not linked to a program, and drills, are not removed by
    deleting a program or season.
  </p>
  <p>
    For anything else, use the <a href="/support#contact">contact form</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How long it takes</h2>
  <div class="scroll-x">
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>When it is gone</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>In the app</td><td>Immediately, before the screen closes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Through the <a href="/support#contact">contact form</a>, if you can't sign in</td><td>Within 30 days, and normally within a few days.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Nothing is retained after deletion for analytics or any other purpose,
    because there is no analytics. Routine encrypted infrastructure backups may
    hold a copy for a short period before rotating out; they are not readable by
    the app and are never used to restore an individual account.
  </p>

</Base>
